.TH UPDATE 1M 
.SH NAME
update \- periodically update the super block
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B update
[
interval
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Update
is a program that executes
the
.IR sync (2)
primitive every 30 seconds.
This insures that the file system
is fairly up to date in case of a crash.
.PP
If the parameter
.I interval
is given, it is used
instead of 30 for the timing interval.
This command should not be executed directly,
but should be executed out of the
initialization shell command file,
.I rc(8).
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
/etc/update
.PP
as invoked in "/etc/rc", does a "sync" system call every
30 seconds.  See sync(1).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
sync(2), sync(1), init(8)


